/* book exam traps: Applying the half-sampling-rate rule to the total converter rate instead of the per-channel rate. One shared ADC divides its speed among all scanned channels, so fmax < fch / 2, not ftotal / 2. | Using 5 V as the span for a ±5 V range. The span is the difference between the limits, 10 V. Using 5 V by mistake gives ΔV half the true value, so the reported resolution is twice as fine as the hardware really is. | Confusing resolution with accuracy. A 12-bit converter has 2.44 mV steps but may be accurate only to 0.1 % of span because of offset, gain and reference errors. */
